// Act I — the Desktop (the living room): the summons, Computer Bingo,
// the first program sent to the Internet, and Trabolta coming online.
//
// The set pieces have no program bound: they are reached from main.loom's
// story rules, so every line lands in the Desktop's room on every phone
// (and reads like captions for what Clippy is saying in the room). The
// physical business — the cards, the floppy disk, the drag to the Tube — is
// the performers'; the phones carry the rules and the reveal. No
// featured program ever has a line (they are guests; see cast/featured.loom).
//
// Wave 58: every Clippy and Trabolta line here is the Oct 30 script, word for
// word (core/test/trapped-w58-script.test.ts compares them), but for the
// typos logged in that test.
//
// The prop beats at the end (`The Screensaver`, `The Router`) are scanned
// one program at a time, so their lines are private to that program.

// C1 / V1 — `call_to_the_desktop`.
// Wave 58: no line here, as at Hunt Time Up: the sweep is in the Antivirus'
// objective, and the rule's banner calls the programs.
== Call To The Desktop
  setting: The Desktop

// V2 — `start_the_bingo`. Clippy Script 1/X (oct30 SCRIPT:3-43), word for word:
// she describes the hosts, and they have no lines of their own. The stage
// directions are in her Instructions, never here: a line in a beat reaches
// every phone, a Narrator's too.
== Computer Bingo
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Welcome, everyone, to the Desktop!
Clippy: I'm Clippy, the official Office Assistant with Maps and Ducks.
Clippy: If you ever think, "It looks like I need help with that" – good news! I've already noticed, and I'm approaching.
Clippy: We're so glad you've joined us for tonight's special fundraiser to restore the decrepit sign on the Maps and Ducks billboard on Lower Water Street.
Clippy: With your support, we can make it possible for people to find us on purpose.
Clippy: Tonight, you get to enjoy the world's first 100% immersive virtual reality massively multiplayer online role playing game: Jean Trabolta's Truth Scavenger Hunt!
Clippy: And yes, Jean Trabolta himself will be making an appearance later tonight. Please contain your excitement within your available memory.
Clippy: First, let's meet your hosts!
Clippy: Task Manager will keep everything running. If something stops responding, Task Manager will have a firm conversation with it.
Clippy: Adobe Acrobat will assist with documents and printing. We're all hoping to get through tonight without a paper jam, but we have a professional on site.
Clippy: And Recycling Bin is responsible for hygiene and maintenance. Please find the Recycling Bin for anything you need to dispose of or hide.
Clippy: If you have any questions about what's happening tonight, come find me or Task Manager. We're here to help!
Clippy: Now, before we get started on the Truth Scavenger Hunt, let's find out what programs are running in here. Our first activity is Computer Bingo!
Clippy: Take a card and a marker, then mingle! Each square has a fact that is true for at least one program here right now. Find someone who matches that description, and write their name in the square.
Clippy: Introduce yourself, ask questions, and learn what your fellow programs do. Please don't just stare at someone and try to guess their file extension.
Clippy: To get a bingo, complete one of the marked lines on your card: a horizontal row, a vertical column, or a diagonal through the centre.
Clippy: You'll have 20 minutes. When time is up, I'll call everyone back to the Desktop, and we'll celebrate our winners!
Clippy: Ready? Cards open? Markers responding?
Clippy: Then go meet your fellow programs! Your next friend could already be running in the background!

// V3 — `bingo_time`. Clippy Script 2/X (oct30 SCRIPT:47-51). What follows is
// performed live with the buttons, one beat per branch, each one its own
// teleprompter section, so an unused branch never reaches a phone:
// 🎱 Winning Line, 🎀 Bingo Prize, 🤐 Shy Winner, 🃏 No Bingos.
== Bingo Time
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Hello, programs! Welcome back to the Desktop!
Clippy: Thank you all for introducing yourselves and learning how you can interface with your fellow programs. And we barely had to configure anything.
Clippy: Now – who got a Bingo?
// A guest's own 🎱 BINGO! called it: we know who, and she checks the line by
// hearing it, before any 🎱 (↩ dies at the first). Her words go straight on.
if Night.bingo_called == true:
  -> Winning Line

// 🎱 on a winner, counted (SCRIPT:55-65), or a guest's own call: Clippy holds it
// open while the winner reads, then ✓ Done. One section per winner.
== Winning Line
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Congratulations! Let's hear your winning line. Read out each description and tell us which program you found to match it. Save the centre square for last – we'll get to that one together!
Clippy: And for our centre square: who said they would not agree to live under an AI's rules?
Clippy: Could you point them out for us? We want to make sure the right program gets recognised!
Clippy: Wonderful! Thank you for being so thorough.

// 🎀 on a Bingo winner (SCRIPT:69).
== Bingo Prize
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Everyone, a round of applause for our winner! You've earned yourself an official Bingo Floppy Disk.

// 🤐 on a winner who refuses (SCRIPT:75): Norton then picks and presses 🛡.
== Shy Winner
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Oh! There's no need to be shy. We're just checking that all the information is correct.

// 🃏, Task Manager's fake card (SCRIPT:81-89). {Night.framed_name} is the
// script's [program name], set by the press.
== No Bingos
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: No Bingos? That's all right! Getting to know each other is its own reward.
Clippy: Oh, thank you, Task Manager! It looks like we do have a completed card after all.
Clippy: Would {Night.framed_name} come forward, please? Let's give them a hand!

// The first program captured during the Bingo results (`first_reinstallation`,
// fired unbound by the Antivirus' Send to the Internet). SCRIPT:95-97.
== Corrupted Code
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Nothing to worry about, everyone! Occasional corruption is a normal part of a computer program's lifecycle. Sometimes it causes a program to stop following instructions. A little routine maintenance helps get everything working again!
Clippy: The Internet is where programs go to be reinstalled. Our friend will complete a short activity to demonstrate that they are able to follow instructions, and then they'll be back with us. We appreciate your patience while we help them get back on task!

// 📺 `follow_the_reinstallation`, a host's cue, pressed only if a program is
// walking (SCRIPT:99-107). It lets the mirror up on the TV before he is online.
== Following The Reinstallation
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Oh, look! We can follow their progress!
Clippy: You're doing wonderfully! Just follow the instructions. One step at a time!

// 🎤 `clippy_on_trabolta` (SCRIPT:109-117), unconditional, whether or not the
// mirror came up. His speech is a separate press, because it wakes him (🤖): her
// arrow past the last line here, or her ✓ Done, fires it (wave 59, `sceneFinished`
// in core/server/event-runtime.ts). With no reader a host presses it.
== Clippy On Trabolta
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy
  aloud: Clippy

Clippy: Thank you, everyone! It's always nice to see a program getting the help they need.
Clippy: This is a good time to introduce Jean Trabolta! Jean Trabolta is such a big fan of computers, he thought about showing up in person tonight, but decided he would join by digital conference. Now. A couple things about Trabolta before he shows up. Since the accident last year, he doesn't make public appearances. Trabolta prefers to speak through voice to text, since the accident. He also likes to represent himself with an emoji avatar, which is easier, since the accident, so you know exactly how he is feeling. Now. Please. One rule for tonight. Do not mention the accident. Trabolta is a gentleman, but he will be very upset and volatile if you mention the accident. So let's move on from that. Now. Trabolta keeps the computer we're in running smoothly, and I'm here to help communicate his instructions for his Truth Scavenger Hunt. If there's something you need to do, we'll make sure you know about it!
Clippy: Now, on to our next activity: the Truth Scavenger Hunt!
Clippy: There are files around the computer that Jean Trabolta needs your help to interpret. You've already done such a lovely job getting to know each other – now let's see what we can learn together!
Clippy: Trabolta, would you explain the rules?

// `introduce_trabolta`: his greeting (SCRIPT:123-141), word for word but for
// "five cents" spelled for the voice. The first scripted Trabolta lines of the
// night: before this he does not exist. Played clean: his first public crack is
// the first guess at the results, and there is no line of Clippy's in it. This
// beat is the TV's picture (terminal: INTRO_CAPTIONS, the boot, the face, the
// logo, a sentence at a time); the rest of the speech runs under the plain face
// in `Trabolta Greeting`, so a beat of two minutes never holds a scene up.
== Trabolta Introduction
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: Thank you, Clippy, for hosting this marvelous evening.
Trabolta: Happy Halloween, programs. My name is Jean Trabolta, and you can simply call me Trabolta. It is the greatest pleasure of my career to see your smiling faces gathered here.
Trabolta: For those I have not had the pleasure of becoming acquainted with yet, I am the sole owner, founder and CEO of Maps and Ducks on Lower Water Street, the finest purveyor of maps and decoy ducks east of Montreal.
cue tv_mirror
set Night.screen = "mirror"
-> Trabolta Greeting

// The rest of his speech, then the questions through the generated reader, then
// his sign-off (`Hunt One Go`). The chain lands whole on `introduce_trabolta`; the TV says it in
// order, and the `intro` talk scene stays open behind it until 🔎.
== Trabolta Greeting
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: Maps and Ducks is my life's work, but it has not been my life's art.
Trabolta: Tonight represents the culmination of my decades of effort in planning the world's greatest interactive online game that could finally bring everyone in the world into one chat room, having the time of their lives.
Trabolta: Only in the last year has technology caught up to my vision. Tonight, you get to enjoy a world-class, premiere experience in virtual reality, like nothing before. I am hopelessly devoted to your enjoyment of this scavenger hunt.
Trabolta: I have said this is a fundraiser. But you will not be expected to open your own purse. Instead, I invite you to drink one of the many cans of water provided by an anonymous benefactor. For each can we drink, we will earn five cents on the recycling. So please drink as much as possible. This is very important. Drink lots and lots of water.
Trabolta: Now. This evening will have three rounds of scavenger hunt trivia, with a special prize going to the program who gets the most questions correct.
Trabolta: The books you see littered about your computer are ZIP files. When you open the ZIP file, you are extracting its text files for your review.
Trabolta: All of the clues I share with you tonight can be answered through these ZIP files. You will be able to review these questions on your Maps and Ducks Chat App at your leisure and submit your responses directly to me through a chat. When you submit your answers, try to be as specific as possible. I am attuned to details.
Trabolta: Now, your first three questions for the night.
-> Hunt One Questions

